# docs/hardware: the source of truth for {{project_name}}'s hardware

The AI cannot see the board. Everything it may say about pins, registers, voltages, currents, or timings must come from files in this folder.

Board and MCU: {{mcu}}
Power: {{power_source}}
Worst-case harm if it fails: {{worst_case_harm}}. Safe state: {{safe_state}}

## Put here
- `datasheets/` for every chip and module (PDF, with the revision in the file name)
- `pinout.md`: each pin, its function, voltage level, and the source page
- `errata.md`: known silicon and module bugs
- `schematic-notes.md`: decisions and open questions
- `bom.csv`: parts, second sources, lifecycle status
- `certification/`: test reports and labels
- `fault-tests.md`: results of power-cut, corrupt-image, and offline tests

## Rules
If a fact is not here, ask. Do not infer it from a similar board. Changes to power, radio, or actuator code are safety-relevant: say so and ask for confirmation before flashing.
